WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:01.408
Thursday afternoon.

00:01.458 --> 00:04.650
Marisol has a nonpayment hearing on Monday at 9:30.

00:04.700 --> 00:09.736
Her radiators have been cold since early November, there's black mold around the

00:09.786 --> 00:12.724
tub, and water comes through the bathroom wall.

00:12.774 --> 00:15.521
The city has already cited these conditions.

00:15.571 --> 00:17.301
Her court file doesn't know.

00:17.351 --> 00:19.526
Dev, the paralegal, has 20 minutes.

00:19.576 --> 00:20.480
This is Hearth.

00:22.173 --> 00:25.859
Vivo en la cuadra mil de Saint Nicholas Avenue, en Manhattan.
<i>I live on the 1000 block of St. Nicholas Avenue in Manhattan.</i>

00:25.959 --> 00:29.645
Tengo corte el lunes 23 de noviembre a las 9:30.
<i>My court date is Monday, November 23 at 9:30.</i>

00:29.745 --> 00:33.431
Los radiadores están fríos desde principios de noviembre,
<i>The radiators have been cold since early November,</i>

00:33.531 --> 00:37.217
hay moho negro alrededor de la bañera y entra agua por la pared del baño.
<i>there's black mold around the tub, and water comes through the bathroom wall.</i>

00:37.717 --> 00:42.890
70% of households in her census tract are Hispanic, so intake works in Spanish.

00:42.940 --> 00:48.178
Google Cloud Speech-to-Text transcribes what she says, and Hearth answers Dev in

00:48.228 --> 00:48.707
English.

00:49.607 --> 00:51.826
Tenants say the radiators are cold.

00:51.876 --> 00:52.928
Inspectors write:

00:52.978 --> 00:55.327
provide access to the heating system.

00:55.377 --> 00:58.763
BigQuery vector search matches meaning, not keywords.

00:58.813 --> 01:03.625
Three open violations on her block, including an immediately hazardous heat

01:03.675 --> 01:06.413
violation the landlord had 24 hours to fix.

01:06.463 --> 01:10.886
But one of the top matches was a mold case that was already repaired.

01:10.936 --> 01:12.377
Vector search proposes.

01:12.427 --> 01:16.397
Our rules decide, and Hearth shows what it set aside, and why.

01:17.297 --> 01:19.193
Dev can challenge any decision.

01:19.243 --> 01:24.213
Citing a repaired condition would hurt her in court, and Hearth explains exactly

01:24.263 --> 01:24.527
that.

01:25.427 --> 01:26.674
Snap the court notice.

01:26.724 --> 01:31.331
Gemini reads the index number, the hearing, and the arrears, never the tenant's

01:31.381 --> 01:31.625
name.

01:31.675 --> 01:35.457
One click puts it into the case, and Hearth rechecks her options.

01:36.357 --> 01:41.188
Four NYC relief programs, each checked by deterministic rules, not guessed by the

01:41.238 --> 01:41.549
model:

01:41.599 --> 01:46.370
income against 200% of poverty, arrears against the cap, an open violation where

01:46.420 --> 01:46.912
required.

01:46.962 --> 01:51.854
Her daughter's asthma is noted for the attorney, never used to decide eligibility.

01:51.904 --> 01:54.987
And the countdown never lets Dev forget the hearing.

01:55.887 --> 01:58.597
As they talk, the worksheet fills itself in:

01:58.647 --> 02:02.925
the records, the defenses, the referrals, and what still needs proof.

02:02.975 --> 02:04.869
The paralegal stays in control.

02:04.919 --> 02:09.009
Edit anything, and download it as a fillable PDF for the attorney.

02:09.059 --> 02:14.152
Every case is saved in Firestore, sorted by the next hearing, with the next action

02:14.202 --> 02:14.717
for each.

02:15.617 --> 02:20.618
Real census and city records, with modeled eviction filings labeled as modeled.

02:20.668 --> 02:22.216
We audited our own rules:

02:22.266 --> 02:27.203
requiring a 311 ticket would skip 37 high-pressure tracts with 33,980 severely

02:27.253 --> 02:32.254
rent-burdened households, so those families are routed to inspections and funds

02:32.304 --> 02:34.108
that don't need an open case.

02:34.158 --> 02:38.967
Built on Google Cloud, so Marisol walks into court on Monday with a defense.
